            <!-- Per-tenant storage policy: hot (local) -> cold (S3, TTL-moved).
                 Two volumes following Altinity's CAS-ready shape
                 (cas_with_ttl pattern from docs.altinity.com/altinityantalya/using_cas):
                 - hot: local default disk, inserts land here (S3 writes are
                   the expensive path; write locally, move merged parts after)
                 - cold: the tenant's S3 disk READ THROUGH its cache wrapper
                   (cache_<tenant>, defined in tenant-cache.xml) so repeated
                   cold reads are served from the local cache disk — the same
                   cached-read path the tiered policy gives its cold volume.
                   The raw disk_<tenant> stays the S3 truth; the wrapper only
                   caches. perform_ttl_move_on_insert=false so inserts never
                   wait on S3; a background job TTL-moves merged parts
                 - volume_priority is EXPLICIT (Altinity's CAS example sets it
                   because some builds fall back to alphabetical volume
                   order, where "cold" would beat "hot"; on 26.8 config order
                   is preserved when NO volume sets it, but once ANY does,
                   priorities must cover 1..N) - explicit removes the
                   ambiguity for future editors
                 - move_factor stays as a disk-pressure escape hatch
                 - prefer_not_to_merge on cold: merges must not rewrite S3
                   objects on every merge fan-in; TTL moves handle decay
                 CAS adoption (Antalya 26.6+) later swaps ONLY the disk
                 definition (type=s3 -> object_storage + metadata_type=cas,
                 shared prefix, no {replica} segment) - this policy and every
                 table's DDL stay unchanged. -->
            <tenant_${tenant}>
                <volumes>
                    <hot>
                        <disk>default</disk>
                        <volume_priority>1</volume_priority>
                    </hot>
                    <cold>
                        <disk>cache_${tenant}</disk>
                        <volume_priority>2</volume_priority>
                        <perform_ttl_move_on_insert>false</perform_ttl_move_on_insert>
                        <prefer_not_to_merge>true</prefer_not_to_merge>
                    </cold>
                </volumes>
                <move_factor>0.1</move_factor>
            </tenant_${tenant}>
